  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001101"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-26-464: The project, 87 East Evelyn Phase I, located at 87 East Evelyn Avenue in Mountain View on a 1.53 acre site, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $6,805,335 in annual federal tax credits, $11,280,802 in total state tax credits, and $36,077,751 of tax-exempt bond cap to finance the new construction of 161 units of housing, consisting of 159 restricted rental units and 2 unrestricted manager's units. Recorded as a note because this funding covers 87 East Evelyn Phase I (161 units), which may be one component of this record.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001678"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Phase One (West Building): 7 stories, 161 apartments (25 studio, 53 one-bedroom, 41 two-bedroom, 42 three-bedroom), 159 restricted at 30% to 60% AMI (41 at 30%, 64 at 50%, 54 at 60%) and 2 manager units, with a child-care center. Phase Two (East Building): 13 stories, 107 apartments up to 80% AMI, with community-serving commercial space; Phase Two tax credit application anticipated in 2027.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001678",
        "SRC-002494"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The architect's page lists 30 Phase One and 12 Phase Two units for the county Rapid Rehousing program, 3,150 sq ft of community resource space and an about 7,000 sq ft play area and facility.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002495"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City council report, Nov. 17, 2026 (consent agenda): recommends moving the $4 million Phase Two share of the city's $8 million loan to Phase One; $1,165,343 already spent on Phase One predevelopment. City report of Sept. 8, 2026: state awarded $57,921,108 in tax credits; city loan at 3% simple interest, no payments during construction.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002494",
        "SRC-002497"
      ]
    }
  ],
